==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Yaminoir''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Yaminora''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
==='''Normal Form'''===
Yamii is by no means a strong unit. The combination of low range, damage, and health results in this unit having very low survivability, while being able to do very little in battle. Basically, Yamii is a much worse [[Bird Cat (Normal Cat)|Flying Cat]] stat-wise, just with different targets. Luckily, the price is low and it can work against some [[:Category:Alien Enemies|Aliens]] with single target attacks or low range such as [[Nimoy Bore]], but can't do much in any other situations, making this Form not worth using at all. Yamii's ineffectiveness reaches new depths against [[:Category:Aku Enemies|Aku]] enemies, who have all sorts of abilities that make Yamii ineffective, from [[Shield]]s to [[Surge Attack|Surges]].

==='''Evolved Form'''===
Fortunately, many of Yamii's first Form problems are fixed with its evolution. The guaranteed weaken is now combined with better health and the [[Resistant]] ability to make a decent tank which can fairly easily support your team throughout [[Into the Future]] and [[Cats of the Cosmos]]. This unit is very versatile when it comes to Aliens and often leads to other Cats surviving much longer, which is a very worthwhile return for their relatively low cost. Yaminoir is effective against long ranged Aliens whose attacks can't be avoided, namely [[Cli-One]] and [[Spacefish Jones]]; however, Yaminoir will not work as well in the presence of traits it doesn't target, as their lack of knockbacks is likely to result in more damage taken if it is reached.

A unique feature of this particular Pixie is that Yaminoir also targets Aku Enemies. Its resistance makes them viable throughout [[The Aku Realms]], where they can mitigate the pushing power of enemy surges as well as greatly lowering the danger posed by some enemies, namely [[Condemned Peng]] and [[Aku Gory]]. The lack of Shield Piercing means that Yaminoir rarely ends up being anything more than a damage sponge, but, considering the lack of easily obtainable alternatives, that is a good enough role to fulfill. Yaminoir's health against Akus is good enough for its cost, but not that high regardless, so players should use this unit as a safety net, or a second line of defence to support meatshields, not as a replacement.

For general use, this Form can be a decent midrange attacker, but their recharge time will result in them being outclassed by more common alternatives quite often, though Yaminoir should still be kept in mind for stages where high cost efficiency is required, or the ability to tank some hits in case of need.

==='''True Form'''===
Now that this Pixie has doubled its base health from its previous form, Yaminora does even better at tanking against their main targets. This upgrade allows Yaminora to participate well in heavy-Alien/Aku stages even at late-[[Uncanny Legends]] difficulty level. Although many competent counters for Aliens exist, the same can't really be said for Aku threats. It is still forced to tank any Surges they spawn, and has no means of dealing with Shields, both of which greatly hinder its matchup against them. Nevertheless, it remains a viable second line of defense when aided by specialist meatshields like [[Ancient Egg: N003 (Special Cat)|Cactus]] and [[Maize Cat (Rare Cat)|Cone]].

Another major improvement is the [[Wave Shield]] ability, which works very well with this unit's high range. For Yaminora's meta, Aliens such as [[Elizabeth the LVIth]], [[Bun Bun Symbiote]] and [[Youcan]], can all be outranged and protect the backliners from their Wave Attacks. Its matchup against [[Axoloty]] is situational because of how much damage it could inflict, so it's better for Yaminora to intercept the Wave at range. Meanwhile, Wave-generating Aku threats, namely [[Wicked Face]], [[Deathkory]] and [[Possessed Empress]], all have Shields that block status effects, but Yaminora is still rather viable since it can either outrange or tank them and stop their Waves dead, creating more room for other unit to operate.

For general use, Yaminora hasn't improved their combat ability, but it is now an excellent Wave Blocker, not needing to be replaced a lot like Octopus Cat thanks to its higher range. The ranged Wave Blocker is still a very rare type of unit in the game, as only certain collaboration ubers ([[EVA Unit-00 (Uber Rare Cat)|EVA Unit-00]] and [[Hatsune Miku: MM2020 Tokyo (Uber Rare Cat)|Hatsune Miku: MM2020 Tokyo]]) and extremely rare gacha units in specific sets ([[Mighty Kristul Muu (Legend Rare Cat)|Mighty Kristul Muu]], [[Gloomy Neneko (Super Rare Cat)|Costumed Witchy Neneko]], and [[Celestial Child Luna (Uber Rare Cat)|Salvation's Daughter Lunacia]]) have Wave Blocker and ranges above 300. It may come with an extremely high cost, requiring 1 Epic Seed and 3 Aku Catfruit, but is well worth the price nevertheless.

==='''Talents'''===
'''[[Shield Piercing]]''' is the highest priority Talent, as it significantly improves matchups against most Shielded Aku. Although a 20% chance might sound low, their Multi-Hit means that it procs consistently enough that you can use them as a solo piercer in a stage.

[[Immune to Curse]] is situationally useful in Alien/Aku + Relic stages as additional assurance in case they get hit by a stray Curse. It can also allow them to tank [[Malevolent Dark Cat]], and potentially pierce their Shield, but it is not particularly advised. As such, this Talent is hardly worth the NP.

'''[[Special Abilities#Resist|Resist Slow]]''' is not useful. It can let them get into Queen B's blind spot, but that's as far as it goes.

'''Attack Buff''' and especially '''HP Buff''' are decent stat boosts, but should only be considered after investing into them with [[Catseye]]s first.

